        <p><b>Day 12:</b> Probability basics -- sample space, events, conditional probability, Bayes theorem. Monty Hall, birthday paradox.</p>
        <p><b>Day 13:</b> Discrete distributions -- Bernoulli, Binomial, Poisson, Geometric. PMF, CDF, expected value, variance.</p>
        <p><b>Day 14:</b> Continuous distributions -- Uniform, Normal, Exponential, Beta. PDF, CDF. Central Limit Theorem simulation.</p>
        <p><b>Day 15:</b> Sampling -- random sampling, stratified, bootstrap. Sampling distributions. Confidence intervals.</p>
        <p><b>Day 16:</b> Hypothesis testing -- null/alternative, p-values, t-tests (one-sample, two-sample, paired), chi-squared. Type I/II errors.</p>
        <p><b>Day 17:</b> ANOVA, correlation (Pearson, Spearman), effect size. Multiple testing correction (Bonferroni).</p>
        <p><b>Day 18:</b> Bayesian statistics -- prior, likelihood, posterior. Beta-Binomial model. Bayesian A/B testing.</p>
        <p><b>Day 19:</b> Information theory basics -- entropy, cross-entropy, KL divergence. Connection to ML loss functions.</p>
        <p><b>Day 20:</b> Integration and project completion day.</p>
