        <p><b>Day 82:</b> Prompt engineering -- system prompts, few-shot, chain-of-thought, self-consistency, structured output (JSON mode).</p>
        <p><b>Day 83:</b> Embeddings -- text embedding models, vector similarity, semantic search. Embedding dimensions and quality trade-offs.</p>
        <p><b>Day 84:</b> Vector databases -- ChromaDB, Pinecone, Weaviate, pgvector. CRUD operations, filtering, hybrid search.</p>
        <p><b>Day 85:</b> RAG pipeline -- document loading, chunking strategies, embedding, retrieval, augmented generation. Evaluation (faithfulness, relevance).</p>
        <p><b>Day 86:</b> Advanced RAG -- hybrid search (dense + sparse), re-ranking, query decomposition, multi-hop retrieval, parent-child chunks.</p>
        <p><b>Day 87:</b> Fine-tuning LLMs -- LoRA/QLoRA on Llama/Mistral. Dataset preparation, training, evaluation. Merge and quantize.</p>
        <p><b>Day 88:</b> AI agents -- tool use, function calling, ReAct pattern. LangChain/LlamaIndex agents. Planning and execution.</p>
        <p><b>Day 89:</b> Multi-agent systems -- agent orchestration, task decomposition, collaboration patterns. CrewAI or AutoGen.</p>
        <p><b>Day 90:</b> Integration and project completion day.</p>
        <div class="do-box">
          <b>5 Projects:</b><br>
          <b>P1 - RAG Knowledge Base:</b> Full RAG pipeline over your own documents (notes, PDFs, code). ChromaDB + OpenAI/local embeddings. Evaluation with RAGAS. Gradio chat interface. Source citation in responses.<br>
          <b>P2 - Code Assistant:</b> RAG over a codebase. Parse code into meaningful chunks. Answer questions about code architecture. Generate code based on existing patterns. Function-level retrieval.<br>
          <b>P3 - Fine-Tuned Domain Expert:</b> QLoRA fine-tune Llama/Mistral on domain-specific data (medical, legal, financial). Evaluate against base model. Deploy on Hugging Face with 4-bit quantization.<br>
          <b>P4 - AI Research Agent:</b> Agent that takes a research question, searches the web, reads papers, synthesizes findings. Tool use: web search, PDF reader, note-taker. Produces structured report.<br>
          <b>P5 - Multi-Agent Workflow:</b> Team of agents: researcher, writer, critic, editor. Given a topic, they collaboratively produce a well-researched article. Each agent has distinct personality and tools.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

