        <p><b>Day 92:</b> Data versioning -- DVC (Data Version Control). Track datasets and models alongside code. Reproducible experiments.</p>
        <p><b>Day 93:</b> Model serving -- FastAPI + Docker. Batch vs real-time inference. Model serialization (ONNX, TorchScript). Latency optimization.</p>
        <p><b>Day 94:</b> Model monitoring -- data drift detection (Evidently AI), performance degradation, feature drift. Alerting.</p>
        <p><b>Day 95:</b> ML pipelines -- Airflow/Prefect for orchestration. DAGs for data processing, training, evaluation, deployment.</p>
        <p><b>Day 96:</b> CI/CD for ML -- automated testing (data tests, model tests, integration tests). GitHub Actions for ML. Model registry.</p>
        <p><b>Day 97:</b> Containerization for ML -- Docker for GPU workloads. Multi-stage builds for smaller images. NVIDIA Container Toolkit.</p>
        <p><b>Day 98:</b> Cloud ML services -- AWS SageMaker / GCP Vertex AI / Azure ML overview. Managed training, deployment, endpoints.</p>
        <p><b>Day 99:</b> Scaling ML -- distributed training (DDP, FSDP). Model parallelism. Inference optimization (quantization, distillation, pruning).</p>
        <p><b>Day 100:</b> Retrospective -- deploy all 3 best models as production services. Write comprehensive blog post. Update portfolio.</p>
        <div class="do-box">
          <b>5 Projects:</b><br>
          <b>P1 - ML Pipeline:</b> End-to-end pipeline: data ingestion, validation, preprocessing, training, evaluation, model registry, deployment. Orchestrated with Prefect/Airflow. Triggered by new data.<br>
          <b>P2 - Model Monitoring Dashboard:</b> Deploy a model and monitor it. Track prediction distribution, data drift, accuracy over time. Automated retraining trigger when drift exceeds threshold. Grafana dashboard.<br>
          <b>P3 - ML API Platform:</b> Multi-model serving platform. REST API with model versioning, A/B testing, canary deployments. Authentication, rate limiting, usage tracking. Docker + Kubernetes deployment.<br>
          <b>P4 - Experiment Tracker:</b> Build a simplified MLflow: log parameters, metrics, artifacts. Compare runs. Model registry with staging/production labels. Web UI for viewing experiments.<br>
          <b>P5 - Production ML System:</b> Full production system: data pipeline + training pipeline + serving + monitoring + CI/CD. Real-time predictions, batch predictions, model updates without downtime. The capstone that proves you can do production ML.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
